{0 Logging}

Standard output and standard error of the OCaml program reach the Workers logs.
Use [wrangler dev], [wrangler tail] or the dashboard to read them.

{@ocaml[
let handler _req _env _ctx =
  print_endline "request received";
  Printf.printf "answering with %d%!" 200;
  prerr_endline "this goes to the error log";
  Workero.Response.text "ok\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

These forms work (checked in workerd):

- [print_endline] and [prerr_endline].
- [Printf.printf] and [Printf.eprintf] when the format ends with [%!].

Output that is not flushed stays in the buffer and does not appear. This
covers [Printf.printf] without [%!], and [print_string] without a newline or a
flush. Flush it with [%!] or [flush stdout].
